{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall have a peg upon your tool.</b> The א is superfluous, and its meaning is 'upon your weapon.' And this commandment was a great distinction and honor for Israel, inasmuch as the Shekhinah walked in the midst of their camps. And it was after they sinned, for before they sinned they did not need it, for the manna was absorbed in the limbs and dissipated also the taste of other foods; but after they sinned they required it. And I have already mentioned something of this in the section of בהעלותך. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted in Yoma, at the beginning of the chapter יום הכפורים: the Tanna — when they relieved themselves, they would not turn to their sides nor to their front, but to their rear. And the meaning is that the clouds of glory spread in every direction before them and to their sides, but they did not pass behind Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:33.743330047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}